## What changed
First of three Phase 3 PRs. Drops the foundation sibling PRs 2 (drag-to-connect + edge label) and 3 (edge selection + delete + color picker + 100×200 perf) build on top of.

**New code**
- `src/renderer/store/edges.ts` — Zustand `useEdges` slice + `makeEdgeId` + `deleteNodeAndEdges` cascade helper. `Edge` / `EdgeSide` / `EdgeEnd` declared locally; fields match plan §5 byte-for-byte so Phase 5's rename to `src/shared/aimap.ts` is import-path only.
- `src/renderer/canvas/edges/geometry.ts` — pure, framework-free math: `anchorPosition`, `defaultSidesFor` (closest-pair, 16-candidate brute force), `bezierControlPoints` (perpendicular offset clamped to [40, 200]), `arrowHeadPoints` (isoceles triangle oriented along the curve's endpoint tangent). Plus `EDGE_ARROW_SIZE`, `EDGE_CONTROL_OFFSET_MIN`, `EDGE_CONTROL_OFFSET_MAX`.
- `src/renderer/canvas/edges/geometry.test.ts` — **21 unit tests** covering literal anchor coords, 8 directional cases for `defaultSidesFor` (cardinals + diagonals + loop), control-point direction signs + clamping, degenerate-input fallback for `arrowHeadPoints`.
- `src/renderer/canvas/edges/Edge.tsx` — Konva renderer; subscribes to `useNodes(s => s.nodes)` so any node move/resize recomputes geometry and the edge stays attached. Plan §5 defaults: `fromEnd: "none"`, `toEnd: "arrow"`. Selected styling = 3px primary purple (`#6965db`); default stroke = ink black (`#1b1b1f`). `listening={false}` for now — sibling C flips it on for selection.
- `src/renderer/canvas/edges/EdgesLayer.tsx` — Konva `<Layer>` rendering one `<Edge>` per item in `useEdges().edges`.
- `src/renderer/canvas/nodes/AnchorDots.tsx` — 4 circles inside the TextNode Group, radius scales inverse with zoom (6px constant on screen). Each Circle's `name` is `"aim-anchor-dot <side>"` for sibling B's Konva name-based hit-test; node id + side are stashed as Konva attrs.

**Modifications**
- `src/renderer/canvas/Canvas.tsx` — inserts `<EdgesLayer />` between Grid and Nodes layers. New order: Grid → Edges → Nodes → Origin.
- `src/renderer/canvas/nodes/TextNode.tsx` — adds a `hovered` useState (Konva pointer enter/leave), renders `<AnchorDots visible={hovered || selected} />`.
- `src/renderer/canvas/interactions/useDeleteKey.ts` — routes node deletion through `deleteNodeAndEdges` so connected edges are atomically removed in the same logical step.
- `DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md` — ticks 3 of 5 Phase 3 exit criteria, adds Phase 3 status block, §10 history entry.

## Why
Edges are the second half of "node-edge whiteboard." Phase 3's exit criteria split cleanly into (a) foundation — the store, the renderer, the cascade delete, the math + tests — and (b) interaction — drag-to-connect, label editor, edge selection, color picker. This PR ships the foundation only so sibling subagents B and C can work in parallel against a stable API. Each sibling PR owns its own files; this PR's exports are the contract.

## Phase 3 exit criteria touched
- [x] Edges never visually disconnect from their anchors during card move/resize/zoom (Edge.tsx subscribes to useNodes; geometry recomputed reactively)
- [x] Deleting a card also deletes its connected edges (in one undoable step) — `deleteNodeAndEdges` helper; Phase 4 history wraps both writes
- [x] Unit tests for edge anchor geometry — `geometry.test.ts`, 21 tests

Still open (sibling PRs / Phase 5):
- [ ] 100 cards × 200 edges renders at 60fps during pan/zoom (sibling C)
- [ ] Save/load preserves edges with labels, colors, arrow style (Phase 5)

